` for the reverse relation's reciprocal cache."},{"id":"explicit_database","verdict":"met","evidence":"The change only calls `queryset._add_hints(instance=instances[0])`; it does not replace the queryset's explicit database selection. Existing using() precedence therefore remains effective. Tests construct `queryset = House.objects.using(db)`, configure a router to select the opposite database, and assert `router.db_for_read.assert_not_called()` and `self.assertEqual(queryset._db, db)`."},{"id":"router_hints","verdict":"met","evidence":"Both additions use `_add_hints(instance=instances[0])`, preserving existing hints through the helper's established contract and leaving database selection to existing routing. No eager `.db` resolution or `.using()` assignment is introduced. Tests begin with `House.objects.db_manager(hints={\"custom\": \"hint\"}).all()` and assert `set(call.kwargs) == {\"instance\", \"custom\"}`, the parent instance's identity, and `self.assertIsNone(queryset._db)`."},{"id":"prefetch_compatibility","verdict":"met","evidence":"The only production changes add instance hints in the two custom-queryset branches; existing filtering, bulk fetching, caching, and many-to-many paths remain intact. Reuse updates the instance hint without binding `_db`. Tests assert `self.assertIsNone(queryset._result_cache)` and unchanged ordering across reuse, `self.assertIs(getattr(room, relation), house)` under zero-query assertions for cached relations, and zero queries for `Prefetch(relation, queryset=House.objects.none())`. Parent-database tests require exactly two total queries for two parents, preserving bulk prefetch behavior."}],"pass":true},"outcome":"5/5 criteria met","results":[{"c":215,"at":2,"t":1,"cut":null},{"c":9145,"at":3,"t":1,"cut":null},{"c":9283,"at":4,"t":1,"cut":null},{"c":10224,"at":5,"t":1,"cut":null},{"c":11640,"at":6,"t":1,"cut":null},{"c":11265,"at":7,"t":1,"cut":null},{"c":10796,"at":8,"t":1,"cut":null},{"c":10727,"at":9,"t":1,"cut":null},{"c":10